<title>JAPAN: Japan lifts emergency pork tariff-farm ministry.</title>
<headline>Japan lifts emergency pork tariff-farm ministry.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan on Tuesday lifted an emergency import tariff on pork put in place on April 1 to limit an influx of foreign pork, an Agriculture Ministry official said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The emergency import tariff was lifted from today,&quot; a ministry official said.</p>
<p>The tariff, in accordance with the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade on agricultural products, came in to effect whenever the average volume of imports reached a level more than 19 percent higher than the average of the previous three years.</p>
<p>The measure pushed up the average import price of pork at port by 24 percent compared to that not affected by the tariff.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
